--
"delete argument must have offset zero" failed: convert_cpp_delete passed
the operand, a pointer to the Y subobject, to __delete.  The front end now
attaches the address of the most derived object, computed as for
dynamic_cast<void *> ([expr.dynamic.cast]/8), to a delete-expression
whose operand points to a polymorphic class, and goto conversion passes
it to the deallocation function.
